seg-0e729ad96db9 = <b>Signal loss is not the sky.</b> When satellites the receiver lists in view (above <c1/>) are not tracked, the engine also derives the DOP of every satellite in view. If that in-view DOP is within the thresholds and either nothing is tracked or the untracked satellites are spread around the horizon (not confined to one half of it), the sky was there and the signal was not: the epoch carries <c2/>, the note "satellites in view but not tracked: signal environment, not geometry", and the geometry deduction is classed <c3/>. Untracked satellites confined to one half of the horizon still read as a blocked sky (a wall, a cliff, a quay). A two-sided obstruction (a canyon or a narrow fjord) reads as signal loss until a skyline is configured. The receiver's no-fix sentinels are not DOP: a stated HDOP or PDOP of { "99" } or more, GGA quality { "0" } and GSA mode { "1" } give no stated DOP.

